course: dictionary
lesson: 7349
title: Learning a new animal word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can learn a new word from the sentences around it. This is called context. «The platypus of Australia is a mammal that lays eggs.» Even if you have never heard of a platypus, the words mammal and lays eggs tell you what kind of animal it is.
explain: The dictionary gives more clues: a duck-like bill, webbed feet, thick fur and a flat tail like a beaver's. «A platypus closes its eyes, ears and nose underwater» tells you it hunts in water. Put the clues together and you can picture the animal.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you are probably right. If it does not, read on or look the word up in a dictionary.
fact: A platypus is an unusual animal from eastern Australia, with a duck-like bill, webbed feet, thick fur and a flat tail.
fact: A platypus is a mammal, yet it lays eggs.
fact: A platypus finds shrimps and worms underwater with the sensors in its soft bill.
fact: It lives in rivers in eastern Australia and Tasmania.
fact: «Platypus» is a noun, and its plural can be platypuses.
exercise: «The platypus of Australia is a mammal that lays eggs.» What does this sentence tell you about a platypus? | It is a bird that cannot fly | It is a fish that lives in the sea | It is a plant that grows in rivers | *It is a mammal that lays eggs
exercise: «A platypus closes its eyes, ears and nose underwater.» Which part of a platypus finds shrimps and worms? | Its tail | Its eyes | Its ears | *Its soft bill
exercise: Where does a platypus live? | Snowy mountains in Canada | Deep caves in Spain | *Rivers in eastern Australia | A hot desert in Africa
test: Hannah reads that a platypus has webbed feet. What does webbed mean? | Having no toes at all | *Having skin between the toes, like a duck | Having very long toes | Having sharp claws
test: In «The platypus, an odd old mammal», what does odd mean? | Very kind | *Strange and unusual | Round and soft | Very fast
exam: Jayden says a platypus is a bird because it has a duck's bill. Is he right? | *No, it is a mammal with thick fur that lays eggs | Yes, because a bill means a bird | Yes, ducks and birds are the same | Yes, it can fly like a duck
